          %p
            In this form, with the assumption that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^d
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Kosinski93"} Kosinski 93, Sec. IX Prop. 5.5
          %p
            More generally, if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^d
            is not assumed to be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin-Thom+construction"} Pontryagin-Thom construction
            still gives an identification of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+classes"} cobordism classes
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normally+framed+submanifolds"} normally framed submanifolds
            with the
            %em
              %a{:href => "cohomotopy#ReducedCohomotopy"} reduced Cohomotopy
            of its
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
