          %p
            (Now the notion of asymptotic directed distance depends on the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+bundle"} normal tangent spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmannian"} Grassmannian
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Gr
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gr_n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %span.newWikiWord
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B SO(n)
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/BSO%28n%29"} ?
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi M
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \subset M SO(n)
          %p
            Both statements, Pontryagin’s and Thom’s, as well as their joint generalization to other
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangential+structures"} tangential structures
            (besides framing and orientation structure) and notably their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead-generalized+cohomology+theory"} Whitehead-generalized
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cobordism+cohomology+theory"} Cobordism cohomology theory
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin-Thom+construction"} Pontryagin-Thom construction
            = succeed "-theory." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MUFr"} MUFr
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+theory"} cobordism theory
            and its application in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Pontrjagin+theorem"}> equivariant Pontrjagin theorem
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Pontrjagin+theorem"} twisted Pontrjagin theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+degree+theorem"}> Hopf degree theorem
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Hopf+degree+theorem"} equivariant Hopf degree theorem
            %li
              %p
